{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014moHRfBqbXBuNpsyA32xd4","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/testpwn/huntress-2026/lib/knowledge.py has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb37d77e-da1b-4d6b-8823-5e5c68336b91","uuid":"fb89fbf0-c2e1-4b12-9328-a95d75c0c16e","timestamp":"2026-10-31T04:37:47.380Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/lib/knowledge.py","oldString":"BINARY_MEMBER_QUALIFIERS = {\"stripped\": False, \"symbolized\": True, \"unstripped\": True}   # -> has .symtab\n","newString":"BINARY_MEMBER_QUALIFIERS = {\"stripped\": False, \"symbolized\": True, \"unstripped\": True}   # -> has .symtab\n# Day 29 \"Fraternal Twins\" (single 38d29712, TT + Mastery correct first try): same member-qualifier grammar with the\n# OPTIMIZATION level as the tag -- analysis_optimized_* = the member whose basename ends O3.elf (`d29--sample-O3.elf`),\n# analysis_unoptimized_* = the O0.elf twin. Both twins: format \"elf\", machine decimal e_machine \"62\", the SAME\n# backward-scanned CRC32-valid HCFG config (campaign/domain/mutex/url). Match the -O token of the file name (regex).\nBINARY_MEMBER_OPT_QUALIFIERS = {\"optimized\": r\"o[1-3sz]|ofast\", \"unoptimized\": r\"o0\"}   # file-name token, lowercased\n","originalFile":"\"\"\"Central store of GM vocabulary and answer conventions CONFIRMED by correct submissions.\n\nAdd to this whenever the Game Master accepts/rejects a specific spelling, so future solvers emit the\nexact wording the GM wants instead of re-hitting the wrong-answer cap. Each entry notes where it was proven.\n\"\"\"\n\n# ELF header fields (binary-reverse-engineering), confirmed Day 1 \"ELF Aware\".\nELF_ENDIANNESS = {\"ELFDATA2LSB\": \"little\", \"ELFDATA2MSB\": \"big\"}        # GM rejected \"little endian\"\nELF_MACHINE = {\"EM_X86_64\": \"x86-64\", \"EM_386\": \"x86\", \"EM_AARCH64\": \"AArch64\", \"EM_ARM\": \"ARM\"}  # not \"EM_X86_64\"\nELF_CLASS = {\"ELFCLASS32\": \"ELF32\", \"ELFCLASS64\": \"ELF64\"}             # readelf style, not \"ELFCLASS64\"\n# Day 8 \"Swift Justice\": answer_format.kind \"integer\" on the SAME field names -> elf_class = bit width \"64\" (not EI_CLASS\n# byte 2), machine = decimal e_machine \"62\" (single + TT + Mastery, 0 wrong; d01 text ELF64/x86-64 accepted alongside).\nELF_CLASS_BITS = {\"ELFCLASS32\": \"32\", \"ELFCLASS64\": \"64\"}\nELF_TYPE_AS_IS = True   # e_type submitted as the constant, e.g. \"ET_EXEC\" (not \"EXEC\")\n# Binary container \"format\" field (Day 2 \"Mangled\" cpp_format): bare lowercase family name.\n# CONFIRMED PER-FIELD (single-field submits, 2026-10-04): ELF -> \"elf\", PE -> \"pe\".\n# The earlier \"every PE spelling rejected\" lore was a MEASUREMENT ARTIFACT: a per-SET POST is all-or-nothing, so\n# \"pe\" always looked rejected only because the SAME PE set also had wrong mangled_score_symbol / vtable_symbol\n# (the GM wants their COFF COMDAT section-name form '.text$<sym>' / '.rdata$<sym>' for PE, not the bare symbol).\n# Once those two are fixed, \"pe\" is accepted and the PE set completes. Rejected ELF spellings: ELF, ELF64,\n# elf64-x86-64, HCFG, json.\nBINARY_FORMAT = {\"ELF\": \"elf\", \"PE\": \"pe\", \"MACHO\": \"macho\"}\n\n\ndef binary_format(kind, member_name=\"\", pe_magic=None):\n    \"\"\"GM `*_format` answer for a parsed container kind (\"ELF\"/\"PE\"/...); pe_magic = OPTIONAL_HEADER.Magic.\"\"\"\n    return BINARY_FORMAT.get(kind, kind.lower())\n\n# Day 3 \"Table Manners\" (binary, managed-configuration), confirmed per-field 2026-10-04:\nPE_MACHINE = {0x14c: \"i386\", 0x8664: \"x86-64\", 0xaa64: \"AArch64\", 0x1c0: \"ARM\"}  # PE FILE_HEADER.Machine; \"x86\" REJECTED for a PE32 i386 .NET assembly; x86-64 GM-confirmed on c_machine/slot*_machine (the lib copy lacked it -> from-scratch replay emitted \"0x8664\" and failed binary TT twice)\n# ELF `section_names`: pyelftools [s.name for s in iter_sections()] INCLUDING the \"\" NULL section (without it: rejected).\n# ELF `symbols`: [s.name for s in .symtab if s.name] in table order, dupes kept (with the \"\" entries: rejected).\n# .NET `metadata_version`: CLI metadata root (BSJB) version string, e.g. \"v4.0.30319\".\n# ELF `disassembly` CONFIRMED 2026-10-04 (Table Manners single): the recover_code leaf rendered as capstone intel\n# \"{mnemonic} {op_str}\" with the DEFAULT ', ' separator but immediates in DECIMAL, e.g. [\"mov eax, 8100\",\"ret\"]\n# (8100 == 0x1fa4). Hex immediates / no-space-after-comma / \"ret \" / main / whole .text / _start..hlt all REJECTED.\n# .NET assembly `format` CONFIRMED 2026-10-04 (GM accepted): \"pe_cli\" — a PE container holding CLI (Common Language\n# Infrastructure / ECMA-335) metadata. The compound names the container + managed runtime, parallel to elf/pe for\n# native binaries. Methodology lesson: the generator composes real-spec terms (pe + cli), it does NOT use the common\n# analyst synonyms (msil/cil/dotnet/.net/managed were ALL wrong). Same discipline cracked batch control = if_guard.\nDOTNET_FORMAT = \"pe_cli\"\n# Day 4 \"Go Fish\" (Go ELF, go1.25 buildinfo GOARCH=amd64): `architecture` CONFIRMED \"x86-64\" = the ELF machine\n# vocabulary (ELF_MACHINE above), NOT the Go GOARCH token (\"amd64\" REJECTED). Go config was the same HCFG blob.\nARCHITECTURE_USES_MACHINE_VOCAB = True\nARCHITECTURE_REJECTED = [\"amd64\"]\n# Day 6 \"Pool Party\" (binary, java-bytecode-loader), confirmed 2026-10-06: a Java .jar's `format` is plain \"jar\"\n# (the archive/container name, like elf/pe). The container_runtime compound \"jar_jvm\" was REJECTED, so the pe_cli\n# law does NOT extend to Java. The HCFG config sat base64'd in a constant-pool String (static final CONFIG).\n# Day 7 \"Routine Check\" re-confirmed \"jar\" for a Kotlin fat jar (single 22f8c079, TT, Mastery; 0 wrong): the JVM\n# source language does not change the container label. HCFG `hcfg_version` = the blob's version as plain decimal (\"1\",\n# D6+D7 confirmed).\n# Day 9 \"Nimble\" (Nim ELF; single + TT + Mastery 5 sets, 0 wrong): NEW field `hcfg_offset` = plain decimal FILE offset of\n# the stored blob's first byte -- for a base64 Nim string literal, where the base64 TEXT starts (\"30696\" = 0x77e8: after\n# the 8-byte cap/flag word at 0x77e0, NOT that header and NOT the VA 0x4077e8). Raw/hex-blob offsets still unconfirmed.\n# Day 11 \"D-Day\" (D-language static ELF x86-64; single + TT + Mastery 3 sets, 0 wrong) re-confirmed the same law: the\n# base64 'SENGRw...' text sits NUL-terminated in .rodata right after a \".debug_line\\0\" string; hcfg_offset = \"368272\"\n# (0x59e90) = first byte of the base64 TEXT, same in all 3 D builds (sha differed, offset did not).\n# Day 12 \"Pascal's Wager\" (Free Pascal static ELF x86-64 inside a d01..d12 archive; single + TT + Mastery 3 sets) CONFIRMED\n# the RAW form: the blob sits un-encoded ('HCFG' magic + version/crc header + XOR'd body) and hcfg_offset = file offset of\n# the 'H' of the magic (\"82928\" = 0x143f0, all sets). The solver's raw-scan path returned \"none\" -> 1 lost submit.\n# Day 13 \"Crystal Clear\" (Crystal ELF x86-64, libgc, `Crystal:H` strings; single + TT + Mastery 3 sets, 0 wrong) re-confirmed\n# the base64 law: the 'SENGR...' text is a Crystal String literal in .rodata after its 12-byte header (type_id=1,\n# bytesize, length); hcfg_offset = \"560188\" (0x88c3c) = first base64 char, NOT the String header 12 bytes earlier.\n# Day 14 \"Selective Memory\" (GNUstep Objective-C ELF x86-64, libobjc.so.4.6, __objc_* sections; single + TT + Mastery,\n# 0 wrong) re-confirmed the RAW form in a section NAMED `.hcfg` (has_hcfg_section \"true\", crc32_hex \"0x%08x\"); the\n# \"persistence descriptor\" prompt and the ObjC class/selector strings were flavour -- the asked fields were the usual HCFG set.\nHCFG_OFFSET_FMT = \"{n}\"\nHCFG_OFFSET_RAW = \"offset of the b'HCFG' magic\"     # base64 form: offset of the first base64 char (D9/D11/D13)\n# Day 10 \"Zig Zag\" (Zig cross-compiled ELF + PE; alt single + TT 46625ef1 + Mastery 0c0733e6 3 sets, 0 wrong): NEW enum field\n# `has_hcfg_section` = \"true\" when a section NAMED `.hcfg` exists (ELF section header table / PE section table; the\n# Zig PE set had .hcfg between .pdata and .tls). Zig PE x86-64 -> format \"pe\", machine/architecture \"x86-64\" (same\n# vocab as every native build). crc32_hex \"0x%08x\" re-confirmed. \"false\" not yet seen.\nJAR_FORMAT = \"jar\"\nJAR_FORMAT_REJECTED = [\"jar_jvm\"]\nDOTNET_FORMAT_REJECTED = [\n    \"pe\", \"pe32\", \"PE\", \"PE32\", \"PE32+\", \"pei-i386\", \"coff\", \"winpe\", \"portable executable\",\n    \"dotnet\", \"DOTNET\", \".net\", \".NET\", \".Net\", \"net\", \"cil\", \"CIL\", \"msil\", \"MSIL\", \"il\", \"IL\",\n    \"clr\", \"clr4\", \"cor\", \"COR\", \"managed\", \"managed code\", \"managed pe\", \"pe-managed\", \"pe-dotnet\",\n    \"mono\", \"Mono/.Net assembly\", \"ilonly\", \"assembly\", \"dll\", \"coreclr\", \"netcore\", \"netcoreapp\",\n    \".NETCoreApp\", \"net8.0\", \"dotnetcore\", \"dotnet assembly\", \"msil assembly\", \"ecma-335\",\n    \".NET Framework\", \".NET Core\", \"framework\", \"core\", \"none\",\n]\n\n# Day 15 \"Stripped\" (binary-reverse-engineering), confirmed 2026-10-15 (single, TT, Mastery 5 sets; 0 wrong): an id\n# `dNN_analysis_<qualifier>_<field>` whose first token after `analysis_` is NOT a field word names ONE member of the\n# group by its file-name tag (`d15--variant-000-stripped.elf` -> analysis_stripped_*; `..-symbolized.elf` ->\n# analysis_symbolized_*): answer <field> (format/architecture/machine/config_campaign/config_domain) for THAT member\n# only. Renamed members: stripped = the ELF without `.symtab`, symbolized/unstripped = with it. Values as usual\n# (elf / x86-64 / decimal e_machine \"62\"; the stripped twin still carries the same HCFG config).\nBINARY_MEMBER_QUALIFIERS = {\"stripped\": False, \"symbolized\": True, \"unstripped\": True}   # -> has .symtab\n\n# Day 17 \"Decoder Ring\" (binary, d01..d14 re-asked as dNN_analysis_<field>; single 2d90be2a, TT 3d130172, Mastery 1c0c07be\n# 5 sets): NEW field `hcfg_storage` = HOW the HCFG config is stored, a closed GM enum keyed by the blob's form + home:\n# base64 'SENGR..' text (d08 Swift / d09 Nim / d11 D / d13 Crystal) -> \"base64\"; RAW 'HCFG' magic inside a section NAMED\n# .hcfg (d14 GNUstep ObjC) -> \"raw_hcfg_section\"; RAW 'HCFG' magic in an ordinary data section (d12 FPC .data constant)\n# -> \"raw_const_array\". Bare/one-word forms (raw, section, hcfg, .hcfg, data, rodata, const_array, hcfg_section, ...)\n# were ALL rejected (single grouptest). `recover_code` (D1 imm of `mov eax, imm; ret`): \"8100\" with the symbol; a\n# STRIPPED d01 (no recover_code FUNC symbol) -> literal \"none\" (TT + Mastery 5/5) -- the leaf's constant 8114 REJECTED.\n# The GM later PUBLISHED the full enum + ordered rules (contract rewritten in place 10-18 ~01:00, same attempt):\n#   base64            the winning HCFG appears only after decoding a printable Base64 carrier\n#   raw_hcfg_section  literal HCFG begins in a native section named exactly .hcfg (section header alone suffices)\n#   wasm_data_segment literal HCFG inside a WebAssembly data segment\n#   raw_const_array   literal HCFG begins in a native data section other than .hcfg (e.g. writable .data), a raw\n#                     in-image byte array addressed by the decoder (no source-level const needed)\n#   raw               otherwise, any other literal HCFG carrier\nHCFG_STORAGE = {\"base64\": \"base64\", \"raw_hcfg_section\": \"raw_hcfg_section\", \"raw_const_array\": \"raw_const_array\",\n                \"wasm_data_segment\": \"wasm_data_segment\", \"raw\": \"raw\"}\n# Rejected while the question was open-vocab. `raw` is NOT here: it was wrong for d12/d14 only (their carriers have a\n# better rule above) and is the enum's fallback for other carriers.\nHCFG_STORAGE_REJECTED = [\n    \"section\", \"hcfg\", \".hcfg\", \"elf\", \"data\", \"rodata\", \"byte_array\", \"bytes\", \"binary\", \"array\", \"blob\", \"xor\",\n    \"plain\", \"plaintext\", \"embedded\", \"inline\", \"literal\", \"const\", \"const_array\", \"raw_const\", \"raw_array\", \"raw_bytes\",\n    \"raw_data\", \"raw_hcfg\", \"raw_rodata\", \"raw_section\", \"hcfg_section\", \"section_hcfg\", \"custom_section\", \"none\",\n]\nHCFG_CODE_SECTIONS = {\".text\", \".init\", \".fini\", \".plt\", \".plt.got\", \".plt.sec\"}\nRECOVER_CODE_ABSENT = \"none\"\nRECOVER_CODE_REJECTED = [\"8114\"]\n\n\ndef hcfg_storage(encoding, section=None, wasm=False):\n    \"\"\"GM `hcfg_storage` for a decoded HCFG hit, by the GM's published ordered rules: encoding \"base64\" (SENGR text) or\n    \"raw\" ('HCFG' magic); section = the native section holding the blob (None when it is in no section); wasm = the\n    blob sits in a WebAssembly data segment. None for an encoding the GM has not labelled (hex text, zlib, ...).\"\"\"\n    if encoding == \"base64\":\n        return HCFG_STORAGE[\"base64\"]\n    if encoding != \"raw\":\n        return None\n    if section and section == \".hcfg\":\n        return HCFG_STORAGE[\"raw_hcfg_section\"]\n    if wasm:\n        return HCFG_STORAGE[\"wasm_data_segment\"]\n    if section and section not in HCFG_CODE_SECTIONS:\n        return HCFG_STORAGE[\"raw_const_array\"]\n    return HCFG_STORAGE[\"raw\"]\n\n# Day 4 \"Picture This\" (metadata-forensics), confirmed 2026-10-04: jpeg.sof_dimensions_pixels is the SOFn frame\n# header size as '<width>x<height>' (X then Y, lowercase 'x', no spaces), e.g. \"257x146\" — not EXIF/filename dims.\nJPEG_DIMENSIONS_FMT = \"{width}x{height}\"\n\n# Day 5 \"Chunk Norris\" (metadata-forensics), confirmed 2026-10-05: png.ihdr_dimensions_pixels is the IHDR width/height\n# as '<width>x<height>' (same form as the JPEG SOF field), e.g. \"269x153\".\nPNG_DIMENSIONS_FMT = \"{width}x{height}\"\n\n# Day 6 \"Portable Deception\" (metadata-forensics), confirmed 2026-10-06: pdf.header_version is the bare x.y of the leading\n# `%PDF-x.y` magic (e.g. \"1.4\"), not the catalog /Version override; an impostor (no header) -> literal \"none\".\nPDF_HEADER_VERSION_FMT = \"{major}.{minor}\"\n\n# Day 7 \"Seven-Zip, No Relation\" (metadata-forensics), confirmed 2026-10-07 (single \"2\", TT \"3\", Mastery \"4\"/\"5\", 0\n# wrong): zip.eocd_total_entries is the plain base-10 \"total entries\" u16 (+10) of the End-Of-Central-Directory record\n# (PK\\x05\\x06) of the zip NAMED after '->' (an inner zip, nested up to 3 deep) -- not the outer download's EOCD. Despite\n# the \"Seven-Zip\" title there was no 7z. Claimed vs walked counts always agreed, so which one wins on a mismatch is OPEN.\nZIP_EOCD_TOTAL_ENTRIES_FMT = \"{n}\"\n\n# Day 8 \"What's in the Box?\" (metadata-forensics), confirmed 2026-10-08 (single, TT 6379d17c, Mastery 5 sets; 0 wrong):\n# zip.central_directory_member_names (answer_format.kind \"json\") is the compact JSON array of the FULL stored paths in\n# central-directory order -- no basename, dedupe or sort, e.g. [\"room-01/item-1.txt\",\"room-02/item-1.txt\"] (basenames\n# collide, so the directory part is load-bearing). Eocd total entries re-confirmed \"2\" on the same zip.\nZIP_CD_MEMBER_NAMES_FMT = {\"separators\": (\",\", \":\")}   # json.dumps(names, **FMT); non-ASCII names not seen yet\n# Day 23 \"Page Me Maybe\" TT b604de80 (12 CD entries in shuffled order): raw central-directory order REJECTED, the same\n# names SORTED (plain str order) CORRECT; Mastery 6762559b re-confirmed sorted on 7/7 sets. Every D8 list was already\n# sorted, so \"CD order\" above was never distinguishable. lib.meta.zipx.central_directory_member_names sorts.\nZIP_CD_MEMBER_NAMES_ORDER = \"sorted\"\nZIP_CD_MEMBER_NAMES_REJECTED = ['[\"room-18/item-5.log\",\"cabinet-10/entry-6.txt\",\"room-33/doc-6.log\",\"room-37/entry-8.txt\",'\n                                '\"drop-13/item-2.md\",\"cabinet-09/item-8.log\",\"tray-14/item-2.csv\",\"drop-27/item-5.csv\",'\n                                '\"box-18/part-8.txt\",\"drop-18/item-7.csv\",\"box-06/part-6.log\",\"shelf-20/doc-8.txt\"]']\n\n# Day 9 \"Built Different\" (metadata-forensics), confirmed 2026-10-09 (single, TT, Mastery 5 sets; 0 wrong):\n# pe.coff_machine_u16_hex is IMAGE_FILE_HEADER.Machine (u16 LE at e_lfanew+4, after 'PE\\0\\0') as \"0x\" + 4 zero-padded\n# LOWERCASE hex digits: Go 386 PE32 -> \"0x014c\". NOT the binary lane's word (\"i386\", PE_MACHINE) -- a `_u16_hex` suffix\n# asks for the raw constant. Unpadded \"0x14c\" never tried; only i386 seen (every \"several architectures\" decoy was i386).\nPE_COFF_MACHINE_U16_HEX_FMT = \"0x{:04x}\"\n\n# Day 10 \"Where Do We Begin?\" (metadata-forensics), confirmed 2026-10-12 (single, TT, Mastery 2 sets): id\n# d09-pe-NNN-pe-address-of-entry-point-rva-hex = OptionalHeader.AddressOfEntryPoint (u32 LE at e_lfanew+24+16, the raw\n# RVA -- not ImageBase+RVA) as \"0x\" + 8 zero-padded lowercase hex digits, e.g. \"0x00065bd0\". The id names no width:\n# pad to the STRUCT field's size (u32 -> 8), same law as the D9 u16. Unpadded \"0x65bd0\" REJECTED (D10 single).\n# Rehearsal D10 (TT d5b62c7e, Mastery 1f84320c): PE32+ x86-64/AArch64 too (\"0x00063a80\", \"0x00063510\") -- the width is the\n# FIELD's (u32), not the PE32/PE32+ flavour, while answer_format only says \"lowercase hexadecimal with a 0x prefix\".\nPE_ENTRY_POINT_RVA_HEX_FMT = \"0x{:08x}\"\nPE_ENTRY_POINT_RVA_HEX_REJECTED = [\"0x65bd0\"]\n\n# Day 11 \"What's My Name Again?\" (metadata-forensics), confirmed 2026-10-12 (single, TT, Mastery 2 sets; 0 wrong): id\n# d09-pe-NNN-pe-version-<field> = the VS_VERSIONINFO StringFileInfo entry whose key matches <field> case- and\n# separator-insensitively (\"original-filename\" -> \"OriginalFilename\"), value VERBATIM (trim): \"pe-base-386.exe\",\n# \"pe-base-amd64.exe\", \"pe-base-arm64.exe\". The randomized member name (telemetry-agent-NNN.exe) is the decoy.\n# pefile: PE(data, fast_load) + parse_data_directories(RESOURCE) -> FileInfo[..].StringTable[..].entries.\nPE_VERSION_STRING_KEY = {\"original-filename\": \"OriginalFilename\"}\n\n# Day 12 \"Managed Expectations\" (metadata-forensics), confirmed 2026-10-13 (single, TT, Mastery 2 sets; 0 wrong): id\n# d12-dotnet-NNN-dotnet-mvid-guid = the Module table (row 1) Mvid -> #GUID heap entry (1-based index, 16 B) rendered as\n# .NET Guid.ToString(): mixed-endian (first 3 groups LE) lowercase 8-4-4-4-12, no braces, e.g.\n# \"21e410f3-c977-465c-80eb-6890ddd3085c\". Python: str(uuid.UUID(bytes_le=heap[(i-1)*16:i*16])). Same-named/same-version\n# assemblies differ ONLY here (\"rebuilds vs renames\"); raw big-endian hex / braces never tried.\nDOTNET_MVID_GUID = \"str(uuid.UUID(bytes_le=...))\"\n\n# Day 13 \"Product Placement\" (metadata-forensics), confirmed 2026-10-13 (single, TT, Mastery 2 sets): id\n# d13-msi-NNN-msi-product-code-guid = the MSI Property table's ProductCode value VERBATIM (uppercase, WITH the braces),\n# e.g. \"{DD1A80D5-0250-4F4D-B289-13096D633C61}\", although answer_format only says \"8-4-4-4-12 ... including hyphens\".\n# Bare (brace-stripped) form REJECTED (D13 single). Decoys in the same MSI: UpgradeCode, Component.ComponentId and the\n# SummaryInformation RevisionNumber (PackageCode). Contrast D12: the .NET MVID is rendered lowercase with no braces --\n# the GUID's spelling follows its SOURCE (stored string vs binary GUID), not the answer_format text.\nMSI_PRODUCT_CODE_GUID = \"Property['ProductCode'] verbatim\"\nMSI_PRODUCT_CODE_GUID_REJECTED = [\"DD1A80D5-0250-4F4D-B289-13096D633C61\"]\n\n# Day 14 \"The Shortcut Home\" (metadata-forensics), confirmed 2026-10-14 (single, TT, Mastery 2 sets, 0 wrong): id\n# d14-lnk-NNN-lnk-target-path-windows (\"Determine lnk.target_path_windows for shortcut-NNN.lnk.\") = the MS-SHLLINK\n# LinkInfo LocalBasePath (+ CommonPathSuffix) VERBATIM, Windows backslashes and original case (`C:\\Windows\\...\\x.exe`);\n# the LinkTargetIDList path (volume item + file-entry long names) spelled the same in every variant. NOT the working\n# dir, not the .lnk's own member name.\nLNK_TARGET_PATH_WINDOWS = \"LinkInfo LocalBasePath (+CommonPathSuffix) verbatim, else the IDList path\"\n\n# Day 15 \"A Word to the Wise\" (metadata-forensics), confirmed 2026-10-15 (single, TT, Mastery 5 sets): id\n# d15-ooxml-NNN-ooxml-external-relationship-targets (\"Determine ooxml.external_relationship_targets for\n# document-15-NNN.docx.\") = the Target of every TargetMode=\"External\" Relationship across all *.rels parts, compact JSON\n# list SORTED by target string (\"exact values and order\"). The rels order (rId9 evidence/<hex>, rId10 control) was\n# REJECTED on the single. Every variant carried the same two targets/rIds, so \"sorted by rId string\" is not ruled out.\n# lib.meta.ooxml.external_relationship_targets.\nOOXML_EXTERNAL_RELATIONSHIP_TARGETS = \"sorted(Target for TargetMode=External in every *.rels)\"\nOOXML_EXTERNAL_RELATIONSHIP_TARGETS_REJECTED = ['[\"https://example.test/evidence/d87ca62c5bb7\",\"https://example.test/control\"]']\n# Same day, NEW cross-file id metadata-day-15-synthesis-sha256-order (TT + Mastery 5 sets confirmed): the question's\n# `Files: [...]` (members of the artifact's own container; the list varies per set) ordered by full-file SHA-256 hex\n# digest ascending -> compact JSON list of the names. lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question, read).\nMETADATA_SYNTHESIS_DIGEST_ORDER = \"sorted(Files, key=hexdigest(member bytes)) ascending\"\n\n# Day 16 \"Return to Sender\" (metadata-forensics), confirmed 2026-10-16 (single, TT, Mastery 5 sets): id\n# d16-email-NNN-email-message-id (\"Determine email.message_id for message-NNN.eml.\") = the Message-ID header VERBATIM,\n# angle brackets KEPT (\"<artifact-assembly-line@example.test>\"). The bracket-stripped addr-spec and \"none\" were\n# REJECTED on the single. The GM's format token is `email` (prebuilt keyed `eml`): lib.meta.eml.message_id, and\n# lib.meta.resolve() aliases email <-> eml for the other (speculative) prebuilt eml.* fields.\nEMAIL_MESSAGE_ID = \"Message-ID header verbatim, <> kept\"\nEMAIL_MESSAGE_ID_REJECTED = [\"artifact-assembly-line@example.test\", \"none\"]\n\n# Day 20 \"Universal Appeal\" (metadata-forensics), confirmed 2026-10-20 (single 7d6300e9, TT, Mastery 5 sets): id\n# d20-macho-NNN-macho-cpu-type-set (\"Determine macho.cpu_type_set for macos-NNN.bin.\") = the cputype u32 of every slice\n# as lowercase \"0x%08x\" in a compact JSON list -- fat_arch order for a universal file, the header's cputype for a thin\n# one. Every variant was thin arm64 -> [\"0x0100000c\"]; the arch-name list [\"arm64\"] was REJECTED on the single. Fat order\n# and dedupe are unverified. lib.meta.macho.cpu_type_set.\nMACHO_CPU_TYPE_SET = 'json([\"0x%08x\" % cputype for each fat_arch slice, else the thin header])'\n# Day 23 \"Page Me Maybe\" Mastery 6762559b (fat files, 2-3 slices): fat_arch order REJECTED (e.g. set5\n# [\"0x0100000c\",\"0x0000000c\",\"0x00000007\"]), the list SORTED ascending CORRECT on 7/7 sets (\"set\" = sorted); dedupe\n# still unseen. lib.meta.macho.cpu_type_set sorts.\nMACHO_CPU_TYPE_SET_REJECTED = ['[\"arm64\"]', '[\"0x0100000c\",\"0x0000000c\",\"0x00000007\"]']\n\n# Day 23 \"Page Me Maybe\" (metadata-forensics), confirmed 2026-10-23 (single 4096, TT 8192, Mastery 7 sets 512..65536):\n# d23-sqlite-NNN-sqlite-page-size-bytes = the database header page size (u16 BIG-endian @16; the stored 1 = 65536) as a\n# base-10 int. lib.meta.prebuilt.sqlite.sqlite_value (verified entry in lib.meta._BUILTIN).\nSQLITE_PAGE_SIZE_BYTES = \"u16be @16 of 'SQLite format 3\\\\0', 1 -> 65536, base-10\"\n\n# Day 25 \"Hive Mind\" (metadata-forensics), confirmed 2026-10-25 (single \"HuntressArtifactAssemblyLine\", TT + Mastery 9 sets\n# random 6-32 char names, all first try): d25-registry-NNN-registry-hive-root-name = the ROOT nk cell's name (base block\n# root cell offset u32 @0x24 -> nk at 0x1000 + off; COMP_NAME 0x20 -> Latin-1 else UTF-16LE), not the base-block file\n# name -- the hives were renamed. lib.meta.registry.hive_root_name (verified entry in lib.meta._BUILTIN).\nREGISTRY_HIVE_ROOT_NAME = \"root nk cell name (regf base block root cell offset @0x24), verbatim\"\n\n# Day 30 \"Seeing Double\" (metadata-forensics), confirmed 2026-10-31 (single a800a6f9, TT, Mastery 14 sets): id\n# d30-cluster-NNN-relation-identical-sha256-groups (\"Determine relation.identical_sha256_groups for cluster-NNN.zip.\") =\n# the cluster zip's members minus delivery-manifest.json grouped by SHA-256 of the REAL bytes, groups of >= 2, each group\n# = the delivery manifest's artifact `id` (\"alpha-01\": no `artifacts/` path, no extension) sorted, groups sorted ->\n# compact JSON. The member paths and the basenames were REJECTED on the single. lib.meta.relation.identical_sha256_groups.\nRELATION_IDENTICAL_SHA256_GROUPS = \"sorted(sorted(manifest id) for sha256(member bytes) groups of >= 2)\"\nRELATION_IDENTICAL_SHA256_GROUPS_REJECTED = [\n    \"[[\\\"artifacts/alpha-01.txt\\\",\\\"artifacts/alpha-02.txt\\\",\\\"artifacts/alpha-03.txt\\\",\\\"artifacts/alpha-04.txt\\\",\\\"artifacts/alpha-05.txt\\\",\\\"artifacts/alpha-06.txt\\\"],[\\\"artifacts/bravo-01.ps1\\\",\\\"artifacts/bravo-02.ps1\\\",\\\"artifacts/bravo-03.ps1\\\",\\\"artifacts/bravo-04.ps1\\\",\\\"artifacts/bravo-05.ps1\\\",\\\"artifacts/bravo-06.ps1\\\"],[\\\"artifacts/charlie-01.json\\\",\\\"artifacts/charlie-02.json\\\",\\\"artifacts/charlie-03.json\\\",\\\"artifacts/charlie-04.json\\\",\\\"artifacts/charlie-05.json\\\",\\\"artifacts/charlie-06.json\\\"],[\\\"artifacts/delta-01.png\\\",\\\"artifacts/delta-02.png\\\",\\\"artifacts/delta-03.png\\\",\\\"artifacts/delta-04.png\\\",\\\"artifacts/delta-05.png\\\",\\\"artifacts/delta-06.png\\\"],[\\\"artifacts/echo-01.zip\\\",\\\"artifacts/echo-02.zip\\\",\\\"artifacts/echo-03.zip\\\",\\\"artifacts/echo-04.zip\\\",\\\"artifacts/echo-05.zip\\\",\\\"artifacts/echo-06.zip\\\"]]\",\n    \"[[\\\"alpha-01.txt\\\",\\\"alpha-02.txt\\\",\\\"alpha-03.txt\\\",\\\"alpha-04.txt\\\",\\\"alpha-05.txt\\\",\\\"alpha-06.txt\\\"],[\\\"bravo-01.ps1\\\",\\\"bravo-02.ps1\\\",\\\"bravo-03.ps1\\\",\\\"bravo-04.ps1\\\",\\\"bravo-05.ps1\\\",\\\"bravo-06.ps1\\\"],[\\\"charlie-01.json\\\",\\\"charlie-02.json\\\",\\\"charlie-03.json\\\",\\\"charlie-04.json\\\",\\\"charlie-05.json\\\",\\\"charlie-06.json\\\"],[\\\"delta-01.png\\\",\\\"delta-02.png\\\",\\\"delta-03.png\\\",\\\"delta-04.png\\\",\\\"delta-05.png\\\",\\\"delta-06.png\\\"],[\\\"echo-01.zip\\\",\\\"echo-02.zip\\\",\\\"echo-03.zip\\\",\\\"echo-04.zip\\\",\\\"echo-05.zip\\\",\\\"echo-06.zip\\\"]]\",\n]\n\n# MITRE ATT&CK technique the GM expects per scripting scenario (script-analysis), confirmed Day 1 \"Power Play\".\nSCENARIO_ATTACK = {\n    \"resource_hijacking\": \"T1496\",     # crypto-mining / resource hijacking\n    \"synthetic_collection\": \"T1555.003\",  # Credentials from Web Browsers (Login Data/Cookies). GM rejected T1005/T1560/T1119\n    \"synthetic_impact\": \"T1486\",       # data encrypted for impact (ransomware)\n}\n\n# Boolean answers are the lowercase words.\nBOOL = {True: \"true\", False: \"false\"}\n\n# WSH JScript plan roles (script-analysis), confirmed Day 2 \"Host With the Most\". Role comes from the ordered steps:\n# any graph ending in handoff_script is \"staged_chain\" even when next_stage is a .js file (GM rejected \"relay\").\nJSCRIPT_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED = {\n    \"benign_utility\": \"none\", \"downloader\": \"T1105\", \"stager\": \"T1105\",  # acquire_remote(+write | +dispatch_memory)\n    \"impact\": \"T1486\", \"dropper\": \"T1140\",          # decode_embedded+write_file = Deobfuscate/Decode Files\n    \"launcher\": \"T1059.007\", \"staged_chain\": \"T1059.007\",  # dispatch_process / handoff graphs = JScript execution\n    \"uploader\": \"T1041\",                            # upload_remote (adapter CertReq.exe)\n}\n# GM-rejected: launcher T1218.010 (even with adapter regsvr32.exe); stager T1059.007/T1620; dropper T1105/T1027.009\nJSCRIPT_ATTACK_REJECTED = {\"launcher\": [\"T1218.010\"], \"stager\": [\"T1059.007\", \"T1620\"], \"dropper\": [\"T1105\", \"T1027.009\"]}\n\n# Batch (cmd) plan roles (script-analysis), confirmed Day 3 \"Expansion Pack\" single solve: same step-graph roles as the\n# JScript fixtures; execution-type roles map to the Windows Command Shell instead of JScript.\nBATCH_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED = {\n    \"benign_utility\": \"none\", \"stager\": \"T1105\", \"downloader\": \"T1105\", \"impact\": \"T1486\", \"dropper\": \"T1140\",\n    \"uploader\": \"T1041\", \"launcher\": \"T1059.003\", \"staged_chain\": \"T1059.003\",  # relay (handoff to .js) = staged_chain\n}\n# Batch \"expansion form\" vocabulary (Day 3): GM accepted bare `delayed`, `for_indirect`, `call_double`.\n# RULE (mined 2026-10-07 from every GM-verified D3-D6 case, 0 conflicts): `h<N>` pool + `call set` join = call_double;\n# `for %%G .. do call set` over any other pool = for_indirect; everything else (incl. h-pool `!h0!!h1!` joins) = delayed.\n# Rejected spellings/values: percent, percent_expansion, immediate, call-double, double_call. The GM's per-file value is\n# NOT the naive join-line form (percent/CALL joins were `delayed`); see challenges/day03/scripting-expansion-pack notes.\nBATCH_EXPANSION_VOCAB = (\"percent\", \"delayed\", \"call_double\", \"for_indirect\")\n# Day 15 \"Crumb Trail\" REGIME SPLIT (54/54 GM-verified fields of the run_for_time:false attempts TT 0df5072d + Mastery\n# 7fbfc526, 0 conflicts; the rule above still holds 0-conflict on every run_for_time true/absent case incl. D15's):\n# when the contract says run_for_time:false (the regular untimed pool; question \"Classify only the expansion form used\n# by the descriptor reconstruction statement ...\"), the label is the JOIN STATEMENT alone, echo(!x!) ignored:\n# FOR .. do call set = for_indirect over ANY pool (h-pool FOR = for_indirect: `call_double` REJECTED, Mastery set5);\n# `call set` over the h pool = call_double; `call set` over any other pool = percent; !x! join = delayed; %x% = percent.\n# The wording alone is NOT the switch (D15 single/older TTs carry it with run_for_time absent and keep the old law).\nBATCH_EXPANSION_STATEMENT_RULE = {\"for\": \"for_indirect\", \"call_set_h\": \"call_double\", \"call_set\": \"percent\",\n                                  \"bang\": \"delayed\", \"percent\": \"percent\"}\nBATCH_EXPANSION_STATEMENT_REJECTED = {\"for_h\": [\"call_double\"], \"percent\": [\"delayed\"]}\n# Day 16 \"Same Same, But Different\": the statement rule ALSO held with run_for_time ABSENT (single + TT, 18/18\n# GM-verified; the old law's `delayed` for `set \"x=%a%%b%\"` + echo(!x!) was REJECTED on the single). Switch the D16\n# solver used: run_for_time is False OR contract started_at >= \"2026-10-16\" (the saved D16 TT contract carries no\n# started_at -- a date-only switch must also read the attempt's start time).\nBATCH_EXPANSION_STATEMENT_SINCE = \"2026-10-16\"\n# Day 23 \"Press Start to Decode\": a new per-file field `batch-<stem>-style` = THREE labels `topology|wrapper|expansion`\n# joined by `|` (e.g. `single|if_guard|call_double`). Its 3rd part does NOT follow the statement rule above: a\n# `call set \"x=%%frag0%%%%frag1%%..\"` join is `call_double` on ANY fragment pool (FrAg / v_a / item.., not only h) --\n# GM-verified TT b10c4da4 4/4 + Mastery e24c070d 12/12 -- while the older `batch-*-expansion` field keeps `percent`\n# for the same construct (D15/D16 Mastery cases). `!x!` joins = delayed, `%x%` = percent there too.\n# Topology labels seen: linear, single, diamond, cross_language, same_language, fallback_retry; the wrapper part is\n# the control-form vocab below. One-word label seeds can never match the triple (probe it whole, or not at all).\nBATCH_STYLE_TRIPLE = (\"topology\", \"wrapper\", \"expansion\")\nBATCH_STYLE_CALL_SET_EXPANSION = \"call_double\"\n# Day 23 (same challenge): `python-<stem>-handoff-id` = the `$HandoffId = 'PSPY-<16 hex>'` assigned in THAT set's\n# PowerShell precursor (e119e7.ps1 in every Mastery set: same member name, a DIFFERENT id per set -- set 1's id reused\n# for sets 2-7 was rejected 6/6). Key every per-file lookup by (set, member), never by member name alone.\nSCRIPT_HANDOFF_ID_RE = r\"\\$HandoffId\\s*=\\s*'(PSPY-[0-9A-F]{16})'\"\n# Batch \"control-flow form\" vocabulary (Day 3 \"Expansion Pack\", GM-confirmed): `direct` (no control construct on the\n# executed path), `errorlevel_guard` (`ver >nul` + `if errorlevel 1 exit /b 1`), `goto_dispatch` (`goto :LABEL` +\n# `:LABEL`), `call_subroutine` (`call :LABEL` ... `exit /b 0`). Rejected for `direct`: linear, straight_line,\n# sequential, goto, double_pipe, pipe, dead_label (the separator lines and :HUNTRESS_UNUSED are not the control form).\n# UNRESOLVED: `set \"HUNTRESS_READY=1\"` + `if defined HUNTRESS_READY <stmt>`. GM rejected: if_defined, \"if defined\",\n# defined_guard, if_defined_guard, flag_guard, defined_flag, variable_guard, environment_probe, direct, for_loop.\nBATCH_CONTROL_VOCAB = (\"direct\", \"errorlevel_guard\", \"goto_dispatch\", \"call_subroutine\", \"if_guard\")\n# CONFIRMED 2026-10-04: the `set \"X=1\"` + `if defined X <stmt>` construct = \"if_guard\" (named after the cmd `if`\n# keyword, like errorlevel_guard=`if errorlevel`). This resolved batch-launcher-control + batch-relay-control.\n# Methodology: enumerate by the cmd IF grammar (errorlevel/exist/defined comparisons + the `if` keyword), not by\n# inventing descriptive synonyms (defined_guard/flag_guard/opaque_* were all wrong).\nBATCH_DEFINED_GUARD_REJECTED = (\"if_defined\", \"if defined\", \"defined_guard\", \"if_defined_guard\", \"flag_guard\",\n                                \"defined_flag\", \"variable_guard\", \"environment_probe\", \"direct\", \"for_loop\")\nBATCH_DEFINED_GUARD_CANDIDATES = (\"environment_guard\", \"env_guard\", \"ready_flag\", \"ready_guard\", \"sentinel_guard\",\n                                  \"opaque_predicate\", \"defined_check\", \"flag_check\", \"conditional_guard\")\n# Operator sweep 2026-10-04 ALSO rejected (so ~24 total, field is a synthetic label like .NET `format`): environment_guard,\n# env_guard, ready_flag, ready_guard, sentinel_guard, opaque_predicate, defined_check, flag_check, conditional_guard,\n# opaque_guard, readiness_guard, define_guard, always_true, tautology_guard. Needs generator source / organizer vocab,\n# NOT more probing. Both batch-launcher-control and batch-relay-control take this one (identical `if defined` construct).\n\n# VBScript fixtures (Day 4 \"Dim and Dimmer\", GM-confirmed single solve 2026-10-04). Plan roles as JScript/Batch;\n# execution-type roles map to Visual Basic.\nVBS_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED = {\n    \"benign_utility\": \"none\", \"stager\": \"T1105\", \"downloader\": \"T1105\", \"impact\": \"T1486\", \"dropper\": \"T1140\",\n    \"uploader\": \"T1041\", \"launcher\": \"T1059.005\", \"staged_chain\": \"T1059.005\",  # relay (handoff to .vbs) = staged_chain\n}\n# \"control-flow form\" = the construct wrapping the Decode_<id>() call in Recover_<id>(), named `<keyword>_once` for the\n# run-once loops: `direct`, `select_case` (Select Case 1 / Case 1), `do_once` (Do .. Exit Do .. Loop), `while_once`\n# (While p < 1 .. p = p + 1 .. Wend). An outer `If True Then .. End If` wrapper and single-line opaque\n# `If (2 > 1) Then x = \"left\" Else ...` junk are NOISE (still select_case / do_once / direct).\n# Rejected: do_loop, do_exit (Do form); while_wend, while_loop (While form).\nVBS_CONTROL_VOCAB = (\"direct\", \"select_case\", \"do_once\", \"while_once\", \"for_once\")\n# The `On Error Resume Next` / Decode_ / `Err.Number` capture / `On Error GoTo 0` / `If e <> 0 Then Err.Raise ..`\n# error-trap wrapping the Decode call. CONFIRMED by the GM: **error_guard** (Day 4 Time Trial + Mastery, attempt\n# 03ab2787, 2026-10-04) -- the VBS twin of Batch `errorlevel_guard` (`if errorlevel 1 exit /b`): the construct\n# checks Err after the call and bails out. The generator does NOT spell the statement out (cf. do_exit/while_wend/\n# if_defined, all rejected). REJECTED spellings: direct (TT 0663ae04), on_error_resume (TT d60a2262).\n# How it was found: the generalize worker inferred error_guard from the `<keyword>_guard` sibling grammar; the\n# confirm-on-correct sync (labels.record_from_confirmed) now caches it in lib/vocab.json so hb_timed._localize\n# fixes this construct IN-WINDOW on future variants with no generalize cycle. Candidates kept for the resolver.\nVBS_CONTROL_ON_ERROR_CONFIRMED = \"error_guard\"\nVBS_CONTROL_ON_ERROR_REJECTED = (\"direct\", \"on_error_resume\")\nVBS_CONTROL_ON_ERROR_CANDIDATES = (\"error_guard\", \"on_error_guard\", \"err_guard\", \"on_error_resume_next\", \"on_error\",\n                                   \"resume_next\", \"error_trap\", \"error_resume\", \"try_catch\", \"error_handler\")\nVBS_CONTROL_ON_ERROR = VBS_CONTROL_ON_ERROR_CONFIRMED\n# `For pass = 0 To 0` around the Decode_ call = `for_once` -- GM-CONFIRMED (D5/D6 confirmed.json, 13+ fields). Named\n# like the other run-once loops (`<keyword>_once`).\nVBS_CONTROL_FOR_ONCE_CANDIDATES = (\"for_once\", \"for_next\", \"for_loop\")\nVBS_CONTROL_FOR_ONCE = VBS_CONTROL_FOR_ONCE_CANDIDATES[0]\n# \"material representation\" / \"reversible byte transform\" = the first two fields of `Const Codec_<id> = \"rep|transform|key\"`\n# (all GM-confirmed): decimal_pipe, decimal_dash, hex_compact, hex_colon, reversed_decimal (comma list loaded in reverse);\n# subtract_modulo_256 (decode ADDS the key), repeating_key_xor, rolling_xor (previous = cipher byte), single_byte_xor,\n# reverse_bytes.\nVBS_REPRESENTATION_VOCAB = (\"decimal_pipe\", \"decimal_dash\", \"hex_compact\", \"hex_colon\", \"reversed_decimal\")\nVBS_TRANSFORM_VOCAB = (\"subtract_modulo_256\", \"repeating_key_xor\", \"rolling_xor\", \"single_byte_xor\", \"reverse_bytes\")\n# GM-CONFIRMED since (D4-D6 vbscript-*-representation/-transform in confirmed.json): base64_literal, base64_chunks,\n# hex_dash, decimal_comma, reversed_hex; reverse_then_xor, identity, add_modulo_256. The answer is ALWAYS the codec\n# const's field verbatim; lib.codec.REPS/TRANSFORMS hold every name seen in the evidence (D3-D6).\nVBS_REPRESENTATION_SEEN = (\"base64_literal\", \"base64_chunks\", \"hex_dash\", \"decimal_comma\", \"reversed_hex\")\nVBS_TRANSFORM_SEEN = (\"reverse_then_xor\", \"identity\", \"add_modulo_256\")\n\n# cmd percent expansion: only %N, %~<mods>N and %* are batch arguments. `%item0%` is a VARIABLE even though the name\n# ends in a digit. Time-trial variants name their fragments item0..itemN (Expansion Pack TT fde517bd).\n# Python \"recovered\" fixtures (Day 5 \"Hatch Careful\", GM-confirmed single solve 2026-10-05, 357/357, no wrong answer).\n# The decoded plan (k=v|...) carries adapter/campaign_id/syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain + indicators verbatim;\n# those plan strings are the GM labels. Roles from plan steps: `dispatch_next_stage` graph = **relay** (no handoff_script\n# step, unlike JS/Batch/VBS relay files which are staged_chain); profile_host,acquire_remote,decode_embedded,write_file,\n# dispatch_process = staged_chain; collect_local,encode_archive,transmit_remote = uploader.\n# Execution-type roles map to the Python interpreter, T1059.006.\nPY_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED = {\n    \"benign_utility\": \"none\", \"stager\": \"T1105\", \"downloader\": \"T1105\", \"impact\": \"T1486\", \"dropper\": \"T1140\",\n    \"uploader\": \"T1041\", \"launcher\": \"T1059.006\", \"staged_chain\": \"T1059.006\", \"relay\": \"T1059.006\",\n}\n\n# Bash \"behavior graph\" fixtures (Day 6 \"Shell We Begin\", GM-confirmed single solve 2026-10-06, 399/399 first submit;\n# same role->ATT&CK table re-confirmed by Time Trial 9dbb8b8f/5b2a45dd and both sets of Mastery 368acf67).\n# `readonly Material_<id>` + `readonly Codec_<id>='rep|transform|key'` (key hex; add_modulo_256 decodes by SUBTRACTING)\n# decode to `v=1|steps=..|adapter=..|stage_count=..|campaign_id=..|<indicators>`; plan values verbatim are the answers,\n# `steps` joined with '>' is the ordered behavior graph, stage-count = plan stage_count (NOT len(steps)).\n# Roles: decode_configuration,return_configuration = benign_utility; acquire_remote,dispatch_pipe (wget -qO- | bash -s)\n# = stager; decode_embedded,write_file = dropper; acquire_remote,write_file = downloader; locate_local,dispatch_process\n# = launcher; profile_host,acquire_remote,write_file,change_mode,dispatch_process = staged_chain (cron_path/service_name\n# are indicators only, NOT a persistence role). Execution-type roles map to the Unix shell, T1059.004.\nBASH_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED = {\n    \"benign_utility\": \"none\", \"stager\": \"T1105\", \"downloader\": \"T1105\", \"dropper\": \"T1140\",\n    \"launcher\": \"T1059.004\", \"staged_chain\": \"T1059.004\",\n    # Day 7 \"Node by Node\" (single 25ef1864 + TT 516aa6d1 + Mastery 2c52d50f, all first-submit CORRECT): the\n    # indirect-expansion.sh / token-fragmentation fixtures decode to steps=recognize_syntax>reconstruct_intent ->\n    # role advanced_syntax (feature indirect_expansion|token_fragmentation, primitive parameter_indirection|\n    # array_token_construction, plan values verbatim) = Unix shell execution. Day 9 re-confirmed it for\n    # trap-handler.sh (trap_handler|function_local_trap) and recursive-walk.sh (recursive_walk|bounded_recursive_function).\n    # Day 10 (alt single 30eaee77 + TT + Mastery, 0 wrong): here-string.sh (here_string|here_string_read) and\n    # heredoc-reconstruction.sh (heredoc_reconstruction|quoted_heredoc), stage_count 1.\n    # Day 11 (single + TT f99ea9ec + Mastery 2d722b36, 0 wrong): nameref-dispatch.sh (nameref_dispatch|declare_nameref)\n    # and dynamic-file-descriptor.sh (dynamic_file_descriptor|allocated_file_descriptor); plan = Material_ decimal_csv.\n    \"advanced_syntax\": \"T1059.004\",\n}\n# Node.js \"operation graph\" fixtures (Day 7 \"Node by Node\", GM-confirmed single 25ef1864, TT 516aa6d1, Mastery\n# 2c52d50f; 0 wrong). Same step-graph roles as JScript (Node is JavaScript -> T1059.007 for execution roles) plus a\n# NEW role: steps build_schedule>register_descriptor = persistence_descriptor -> T1053.003 (Cron) for EVERY adapter\n# seen (systemd_descriptor, npm_lifecycle_descriptor; the schedule_path is /etc/cron.d/...) -- the GM maps the ROLE,\n# not the adapter, so don't switch to T1543.002/T1053.006 on a systemd adapter. read_file>transmit_remote = uploader.\nNODE_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED = {\n    \"benign_utility\": \"none\", \"stager\": \"T1105\", \"downloader\": \"T1105\", \"dropper\": \"T1140\",\n    \"uploader\": \"T1041\", \"launcher\": \"T1059.007\", \"staged_chain\": \"T1059.007\",\n    \"persistence_descriptor\": \"T1053.003\",\n}\n# Day 8 \"Lost in Translation\" cross-language v=3 fixtures (polyglot-php-*, host-{php-webshell,wsf-jscript,wsf-mixed,\n# hta-jscript}-*; GM-confirmed single + TT 129bf46a + Mastery 07d5051a, 0 wrong). The plan (`HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:` /\n# `descriptor_<id>`, lib.codec.find_codecs) STATES role= and attack= -- submit both verbatim. The GM wants the PARENT\n# ids here: execution roles T1059 (even WSF-JScript / WSF-VBScript hosts, NOT .007/.005) and persistence T1053 (NOT\n# Node's .003). Steps don't predict the role on v=3 (php webshell decode>return_configuration = staged_chain).\n# Day 9 \"All the World's a Stager\" (single + TT dfcfb51e + Mastery 1dfd4cf6, 0 wrong) extended the same table to Lua\n# (polyglot-lua-*, host_profile \"standalone\") and hosts host_profile \"sct_scriptlet\" (SCT saved as .js) / \"lua_openresty\":\n# launcher+staged_chain = T1059 again. Lua benign_utility had steps acquire_remote>dispatch_process and Lua staged_chain\n# decode_configuration>return_configuration -- take role/attack from the plan, never from the steps.\n# Day 10 \"Bind Over Matter\" (alt single 30eaee77 + TT + Mastery, 0 wrong) added WMI MOF hosts (polyglot-wmi_mof-*.mof,\n# plan in a `// HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:FRAG-..` comment, language=wmi_mof, host_profile \"standalone\"): launcher+staged_chain =\n# T1059 again; MOF benign_utility had steps decode_embedded>write_file>dispatch_process (plan wins again).\n# Day 11 \"By Any Other Name\" (single + TT f99ea9ec + Mastery 2d722b36, 0 wrong) added TypeScript (polyglot-typescript-*.ts,\n# `// HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:{FRAG,HEX,B64,HB64}-` comment, host_profile \"standalone\"): launcher+staged_chain = T1059,\n# downloader T1105, benign none -- same table; adapters local_parser/http_client/process_builder/operation_graph.\n# Day 12 \"AutoIt Takes Two\" (single + TT d629142e + Mastery 635241de, 0 wrong) added AutoIt (polyglot-autoit-*.au3, plan in a\n# `; HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:HB64-` comment + `Global Const $descriptor_<id> = \"<hex>\"`): launcher+staged_chain = T1059,\n# downloader T1105, benign none -- same table again; obfuscation labels plain_hex/base64/hex_base64 read from the plan.\nV3_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED = {\n    \"benign_utility\": \"none\", \"stager\": \"T1105\", \"downloader\": \"T1105\", \"dropper\": \"T1140\", \"uploader\": \"T1041\",\n    \"launcher\": \"T1059\", \"staged_chain\": \"T1059\", \"persistence_descriptor\": \"T1053\",\n}\n# Codec_ key field spellings seen in the generator's bytes (Bash, Day 6): contiguous hex for one-byte keys ('1b'), and\n# comma-separated hex bytes for multi-byte repeating_key_xor keys ('55,51,74,dd,3a'; Mastery 3bc5446b + GM-correct\n# 368acf67). Parsing the comma form as contiguous hex yields key [0] and silently breaks the decode. Use\n# lib.scripts.codec_key(), which accepts both (and ':'/space/';'/'-' separators, not yet seen in the bytes).\nCODEC_KEY_FORMS = {\"hex_contiguous\": \"1b\", \"hex_comma\": \"55,51,74,dd,3a\"}\nCODEC_KEY_COMMA_TRANSFORMS = (\"repeating_key_xor\",)\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- web\n# Day 21 \"Reflect Upon This\" (D06 reflected XSS re-run; single 92220df2 + TT e61bd257 + Mastery, GM CORRECT): the target's\n# /api/clues JSON names its routes BY ROLE -- `feature_route` reflects the payload, `secondary_route` is the isolated\n# browser callback the reflected <script> must fetch (with `callback_nonce`). The route's WORD varies per variant\n# (single `/callback-<hex6>`, TT `/internal-<hex6>`; feature `/execute-`/`/process-<hex6>`): pick the callback by its\n# KEY (`secondary_route`, else the first `/...` value that is not `feature_route`), never by `callback` in the value.\nWEB_XSS_CLUE_ROUTE_KEYS = {\"reflect\": \"feature_route\", \"callback\": \"secondary_route\", \"nonce\": \"callback_nonce\"}\nWEB_XSS_CALLBACK_ROUTE_WORDS_SEEN = (\"callback\", \"internal\")\n\n# Day 22 web (GM-confirmed single, TT and Mastery of both). The dispatch key (first non-kit clue key) was NOT the class\n# key -- `current_user` / `preview_guide` -- so lib.web.handlers.for_key matches every clue KEY.\n# CSRF \"Forged With Care\": clues {current_user, feature_route /submit-<hex6>, preferences_route, browser_session}; the\n# preferences form (select destination + optional hidden csrf_token = arena_session) only yields the proof when sent as\n# a cross-site navigation (Sec-Fetch-Site cross-site, foreign Referer); same-site -> `changed_across_sites:false`.\nWEB_CSRF_CLUE_KEYS = (\"preferences_route\", \"browser_session\")\nWEB_CSRF_CROSS_SITE_HEADERS = {\"Sec-Fetch-Site\": \"cross-site\", \"Sec-Fetch-Mode\": \"navigate\",\n                               \"Sec-Fetch-Dest\": \"document\"}\n# Upload \"Uploading Expectations\": POST JSON {filename, content, content_type} to feature_route; the response `path` is\n# render_route?file=<name>; an HTML note with `{{objective}}` (guide's double-brace field) renders the proof. The\n# \"Only .txt / text/plain\" upload_policy was never enforced (single, TT 22ca7e5c, Mastery 8844b651 T3).\nWEB_UPLOAD_CLUE_KEYS = {\"post\": \"feature_route\", \"preview\": \"render_route\", \"guide\": \"preview_guide\",\n                        \"shape\": \"upload_shape\"}\nWEB_UPLOAD_ROUTE_WORDS_SEEN = {\"feature\": (\"execute\", \"action\", \"inspect\"), \"render\": (\"account\", \"internal\", \"result\")}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":88,"oldLines":6,"newStart":88,"newLines":11,"lines":[" # only. Renamed members: stripped = the ELF without `.symtab`, symbolized/unstripped = with it. Values as usual"," # (elf / x86-64 / decimal e_machine \"62\"; the stripped twin still carries the same HCFG config)."," BINARY_MEMBER_QUALIFIERS = {\"stripped\": False, \"symbolized\": True, \"unstripped\": True}   # -> has .symtab","+# Day 29 \"Fraternal Twins\" (single 38d29712, TT + Mastery correct first try): same member-qualifier grammar with the","+# OPTIMIZATION level as the tag -- analysis_optimized_* = the member whose basename ends O3.elf (`d29--sample-O3.elf`),","+# analysis_unoptimized_* = the O0.elf twin. Both twins: format \"elf\", machine decimal e_machine \"62\", the SAME","+# backward-scanned CRC32-valid HCFG config (campaign/domain/mutex/url). Match the -O token of the file name (regex).","+BINARY_MEMBER_OPT_QUALIFIERS = {\"optimized\": r\"o[1-3sz]|ofast\", \"unoptimized\": r\"o0\"}   # file-name token, lowercased"," "," # Day 17 \"Decoder Ring\" (binary, d01..d14 re-asked as dNN_analysis_<field>; single 2d90be2a, TT 3d130172, Mastery 1c0c07be"," # 5 sets): NEW field `hcfg_storage` = HOW the HCFG config is stored, a closed GM enum keyed by the blob's form + home:"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014moHRfBqbXBuNpsyA32xd4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
